  "summary": "The aesthetic tradition of exposing photographic film or paper to light multiple times to create superimposed images.",
  "description": "Creates ghostly, layered, and often dreamlike images with overlapping elements, transparency effects, and unexpected combinations due to the superimposition of multiple exposures; this occurs when the film or paper is exposed to light more than once without being developed in between. Popularized in fine art photography, experimental cinema, and later embraced by digital photographers and social media for its ethereal, romantic qualities.",
